From 3d8fe45f8591800538eedaa2445ec4b16ed2502a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alin Ciciu <periqlesfpv@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:29:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm64: dts: orangepizero3w: keep CSI camera rail always
 on

BLDO2 (VCC_3V3_CSI per the board schematic) feeds the CSI camera
connectors, but no device-tree consumer references it, so the unused-
regulator sweep powers it down about 30 seconds after boot. Sensor I2C
detection still works (it happens before the sweep), which makes the
failure look like a driver bug: sensor found, /dev/video0 present, zero
frames, zero interrupts.

Mark the rail always-on. The cleaner long-term fix is a proper
sensor0_iovdd-supply reference (the vendor sensor helper already
consumes it); keeping this minimal until that path is validated.

Verified on Orange Pi Zero 3W with IMX219 on CAM1: without this,
capture is dead after the sweep; with it (and only bldo2 - dldo2/eldo2
were tested and are unrelated), streaming works across reboots.

Signed-off-by: Alin Ciciu <periqlesfpv@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts   | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
index 258878289..7b6755832 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
@@ -2245,6 +2245,15 @@ reg_bldo1: bldo1 {
 				regulator-enable-ramp-delay = <1000>;
 			};
 			reg_bldo2: bldo2 {
+				/*
+				 * VCC_3V3_CSI: feeds the CSI camera connectors
+				 * (schematic sheets 6/13). No DT consumer
+				 * references it yet, so without this the
+				 * unused-regulator sweep powers it down ~30s
+				 * after boot and capture goes dead while sensor
+				 * I2C detection still works.
+				 */
+				regulator-always-on;
 				regulator-name = "axp8191-bldo2";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <500000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <3400000>;
-- 
